# What `project/guidance.py` and `project/rules.py` rendered for `AGENTS.md` and `docs/architecture.md`
# before their standing text moved out of Python string literals and into `assets/guidance/`, as SHA-256
# over the UTF-8 bytes of each page.
#
# The move is only worth doing if it changed nothing a project receives, and "generate before and after"
# cannot be run across one commit. So these were captured on the commit slice 16.3 was written on top of,
# and the new path has to reproduce them exactly (`tests/test_guidance_prose.py`, which also says what the
# matrix below does and does not span). Anyone can re-take the same reading:
#
#     SLIPWAI_LANGUAGES=$PWD/packages PYTHONPATH=src:tests python3 -c \
#         "import test_guidance_prose as t; print(t.record(), end='')"
#
# and compare it with the lines below.
#
# Two profiles, four targets, two deployment shapes and twelve projects, chosen against the conditional
# blocks either page has rather than against plausibility; `docs/architecture.md` is given neither a target
# nor a shape, so it is recorded once per profile and project. Every service is `toy-plain`, because that is
# the one backend `packages/` pins here — so these digests say the pages did not move, not that three
# backends' pages did not move.
#
# A deliberate edit to either page changes these, which is the point: the line a reviewer has to see change
# is the one saying which page's bytes a wording change moved. Re-take them the same way after the edit, and
# say in the commit which page was reworded.
#
# <sha256>  <profile>/<project>[/<target>/<shape>]  <path in the generated project>

#
# Re-taken for the scheduling rules — two bands, a state per slice, refill at every boundary, a `question`
# deck-log kind (`changelog.d/sail-scheduling-is-a-state.md`). Only the rows named there moved:
# `AGENTS.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for mutation once per capability, bounded (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-mutation-once-per-capability.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `AGENTS.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
# Re-taken 2026-10-17 for changelog.d/capability-gates-once-per-capability.md: the rows for `AGENTS.md` moved, deliberately — converge, gaps, design review, adversary, mutation and the hand's walk run once per capability, and three of them moved off the slice.
